---
import AppShot from './AppShot.astro';
import catchup from '../../assets/app/catchup-dark.png';
import { PRODUCT_NAME } from '../../config';
---
<section class="s wrap rule fs" id="catch-up" data-name="Catch up" aria-labelledby="c-h">
  <div class="feat">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="c-h">See what happened <span class="soft">since you last looked.</span></h2>
      <p>{PRODUCT_NAME} remembers the commit you were caught up to, not a clock. It shows everything that reached main after it, grouped by issue or by area, so twenty PRs read as four pieces of work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="halo"><AppShot src={catchup} class="fade-out" alt="Catch up: the pull requests that reached main since your checkpoint, by day, with the newest open in the reader" /></div>
    <div class="facts3 facts4">
      <div><h4>Counts at a glance</h4><p>Merged, stuck and ready, plus main's CI with GitHub connected.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Any starting point</h4><p>Your last checkpoint, yesterday, last week or a tag.</p></div>
      <div><h4>One PR at a time</h4><p>Walk through what landed with <kbd>⇧↵</kbd>.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Agent work, marked</h4><p>Agent-made branches get a badge. <kbd>A</kbd> shows only them.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
